From faa0257be77c3fbf2cb6507a61f6a033165faf90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P Arun Kumar Reddy <arunpapannagari23@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:02:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] libocp: add standalone ocp-recovery-tool

Add a CLI11-based command-line front end for libocp, for bring-up and
scripted recovery of devices parked in their recovery ROM without any
D-Bus involvement. The command surface follows the established OCP
recovery tooling conventions (case-insensitive subcommands, decoded
status output, CMS log retrieval):

  ocp-recovery-tool -b BUS -s ADDR [options] SUBCOMMAND

  GetDeviceID          read and dump the DEVICE_ID record
  GetDeviceStatus      decode PROT_CAP, device status, protocol error
                       and the recovery reason code
  GetRecoveryStatus    decode RECOVERY_STATUS and the image index
  SetForceRecovery     reset the device into recovery mode
  PerformOCPRecovery   recover with -i IMAGE (repeatable; each image is
                       staged into the CMS and activated in order, then
                       RECOVERY_STATUS is polled for success). Exits 1
                       (skipped) when the device is already operational.
  GetCMSLogs           dump a CMS log window (-w, default 2) to a file
                       via chunked INDIRECT_DATA reads, bounded by the
                       INDIRECT_STATUS region size

The tool is gated by the new 'ocp-recovery-tool' meson feature and
installs to bindir.

Tested: on nvl32-obmc against a GB202 GPU recovery target:
  # ocp-recovery-tool -b 50 -s 0x69 GetDeviceStatus
  PROT_CAP: magic='OCP RECV' version=1.0 caps=0x01bb cms=3
  Device status:   0x01 (device healthy)
  Protocol error:  0x00 (no protocol error)
  Recovery reason: 0x0000 (no boot failure detected)

Change-Id: I4d53e48d0e84bd0a5d6103649201eaeb63f60ab4
Signed-off-by: P Arun Kumar Reddy <arunpapannagari23@gmail.com>

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/+/92451]
